From a31b8cb89beb0ac4ca2b1fd0bfb999d05a320441 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 05:33:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Tests on CUDA in float

The tests of the behaviours integrated on a GPU (GenericParallelCUDATest,
FieldOperationsCUDATest, FunctionTest-cuda) compile and pass with float:
- types: real instead of double for the maximum differences, the
  constants and the angles of the rotations (no narrowing conversion);
- the tolerances written for double are bounded by tests/Tolerance.hxx,
  and given explicitly for float from the differences measured between the
  host and the device (contractions of the floating point operations):
  stresses 4.8e-7 (relative to 1e8), internal state variables 2.4e-7 and
  tangent operators 2.5e-5 (relative to 1e10) in GenericParallelCUDATest,
  stresses 9.5e-6 and tangent operators 4.9e-6 for the views on the
  device, about ten times these values;
- the integration cycle of FieldOperationsCUDATest makes three steps in
  float instead of four: at the fourth one, the integration of the most
  loaded points of Norton fails on the host as on the device (stress of
  about 3e9 Pa, exponent 8.2, the residual of the implicit scheme can't
  reach its criterion). The status of each step is now checked to be a
  success, which the comparison of the states requires.
Double: 51/51 (tests on CUDA included); float: 51/51.
